year 2012+(2012-[important past date > 200 years ago])
The world has fallen into disarray for one reason or another
standard post-apocalyptic ideas of cults and bandits
one cult has risen to the forefront of the minds of people
they worship a strange blue and grey square consisting of plastic and metal
it has strange writing on it that nobody can understand

ch1:
the scientist wants to be able to witness a cool event in the past, and
    tries to travel to then, but he messes up the time difference
    since the time machine works with relative dates, not absolute ones.
He ends up choosing a time in the future where the world has gone awry.
He comes across a group of people who welcome him into their way of life
    as he is an outsider and this group are strangely accepting of new
    people.
during his tour of the place, he is shown the worshipped relic which
    he instantly recognises as a 3.5" floppy.
they asks them why he knows about the relic and after he tells them that
    it's a floppy disk, they hail him as a godlike figure since he is
    familiar with the relic.
being the curious man he is, he wants to get hold of the relic to see what
    is stored on the relic held so dearly by so many people.



year 2012
following advancements made by fellow scientists in the field, one scientist
    finds a way to travel to times before AND after the creation of the time
    machine
through a series of fuckups and general ineptitude, he manages to find himself
    in the post-apoc. world (he meant to go back but went forward)
the chapter 1 story is about his discovery of the cult's trophy (a floppy disk
    of this game)

